        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted max-w-2xl mx-auto text-lg">dark-memory-mcp is not another library: it is the backbone of how we write code. Governance-as-code, not governance-as-policy.</p>
      </div>

<!-- 3 visual steps: spec → judge → publish -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-14">
        <!-- Step 1: Spec -->
        <div class="glass rounded-sm p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-sm bg-corporate-100 border border-corporate-700/30 flex items-center justify-center">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-corporate-800" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z"></path></svg>
            </div>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-text-faint">[01]</span>
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-display font-bold text-text-base mb-2">You write the spec</h4>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">Before a single line of code, the intent is documented in OpenSpec with tasks, dependencies, and acceptance criteria.</p>
          <div class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs bg-[#0d0d12] border border-border-base rounded-sm p-3 overflow-x-auto">
            <span class="text-corporate-800">dark_memory</span>.<span class="text-yellow-200">vibe_spec</span>(&#123; vibe_case: <span class="text-status-online">'C1'</span>, tasks: <span class="text-text-faint">[...]</span> &#125;)
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 2: Judge -->
        <div class="glass rounded-sm p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-sm bg-corporate-100 border border-corporate-700/30 flex items-center justify-center">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-corporate-800" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 6l3 1m0 0l-3 9a5.002 5.002 0 006.001 0L6 7m3-1L6 7m0 0L3 6m6-1L6 7m0 0L3 6m9 1h6m-6 4h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z"></path></svg>
            </div>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-text-faint">[02]</span>
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-display font-bold text-text-base mb-2">A judge audits the artifact</h4>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">LLM-as-judge, not LLM-as-author. Every artifact is compared against its spec and gets a verdict: aligned, drift_detected, or needs_human.</p>
          <div class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs bg-[#0d0d12] border border-border-base rounded-sm p-3 overflow-x-auto">
            <span class="text-text-faint">// verdict persisted to judgment_history</span><br/>
            <span class="text-corporate-800">verdict</span>: <span class="text-status-online">'aligned'</span> · conf <span class="text-yellow-200">0.98</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 3: Publish -->
        <div class="glass rounded-sm p-6">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
            <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-sm bg-status-online/10 border border-status-online/30 flex items-center justify-center">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-status-online" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"></path></svg>
            </div>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-text-faint">[03]</span>
          </div>
          <h4 class="font-display font-bold text-text-base mb-2">You publish with transparency</h4>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">The whole cycle lands in write_audit: who wrote, which spec, which judge, which verdict. Nothing ships without a trace.</p>
          <div class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs bg-[#0d0d12] border border-border-base rounded-sm p-3 overflow-x-auto">
            <span class="text-status-online">✓ drift: aligned</span> · <span class="text-text-faint">write_audit #5572</span>
